dules or edit lib.rs).\n\nNotes:\n- Reference build: Linux/glibc x86-64. `_WIN32`, `__native_client__`, `__EMSCRIPTEN__`,\n  `__wasi__`, `__OpenBSD__`, `__CloudABI__`, `NONBLOCKING_RANDOM` are undefined.\n  No config.h, so `HAVE_GETENTROPY`, `HAVE_GETRANDOM`, `HAVE_SYS_RANDOM_H`,\n  `HAVE_LINUX_RANDOM_H`, `HAVE_PTHREAD`, `HAVE_POLL`, `HAVE_SAFE_ARC4RANDOM`,\n  `HAVE_GETPID`, `HAVE_NANOSLEEP` are UNDEFINED.\n  RUN THE PREPROCESSOR and translate exactly the surviving code:\n    gcc -E -Ic_src/libsodium/include -Ic_src/libsodium/include/sodium \\\n        -Ic_src/libsodium/randombytes c_src/libsodium/randombytes/sysrandom/randombytes_sysrandom.c > $TMPDIR/sysrandom.i\n    gcc -E -Ic_src/libsodium/include -Ic_src/libsodium/include/sodium \\\n        -Ic_src/libsodium/randombytes c_src/libsodium/randombytes/internal/randombytes_internal_random.c > $TMPDIR/intrandom.i\n    gcc -E -Ic_src/libsodium/include -Ic_src/libsodium/include/sodium \\\n        -Ic_src/libsodium/randombytes c_src/libsodium/randombytes/randombytes.c > $TMPDIR/rb.i\n  and read those files. Do not guess which branch is taken.\n- You will need raw syscalls / libc functions: `open`, `read`, `close`, `poll`, `abort`,\n  `malloc`, `free`, `getpid`, `nanosleep`, `sysconf`, `mmap`... Declare whichever ones the\n  surviving C code needs in local `extern \"C\"` blocks (there is NO `libc` crate). `std`\n  is available and you may use `std::fs`/`std::io` internally if behaviour is identical,\n  but raw `extern \"C\"` declarations are usually the most faithful.\n- `randombytes_internal_random.c` uses ChaCha20 (`crypto_stream_chacha20`) and/or\n  `crypto_core_salsa20` and `crypto_stream_salsa20`; those are defined in other C files —\n  declare them via local `extern \"C\"` blocks. Check the preprocessed output for the exact\n  functions referenced.\n- `sodium_misuse`, `sodium_memzero`, `sodium_malloc`, `sodium_free`, `sodium_mlock`,\n  `sodium_munlock`, `sodium_stackzero` come from sodium/utils.c — declare via\n  `