 (from `c_src/libsodium/crypto_verify/verify.c`)\n\nExported symbols (6):\n- `crypto_verify_16`, `crypto_verify_16_bytes`, `crypto_verify_32`, `crypto_verify_32_bytes`, `crypto_verify_64`, `crypto_verify_64_bytes`\n\nPrivate items: `crypto_verify_n` (the portable `#else` branch, since `HAVE_EMMINTRIN_H`/`__SSE2__` are undefined) and `static optblocker_u16: AtomicU16` — confirmed absent from the dynamic symbol table.\n\nThe arithmetic is reproduced exactly, with `d` modelled as a `u16` accessed through `read_volatile`/`write_volatile` (mirroring C's `volatile uint16_t`), and `x[i]`/`y[i]` read via `read_volatile`. `d--` uses `wrapping_sub(1)`. The final `((d >> 13) ^ optblocker_u16) >> 2` is computed in `u32` to mirror C's integer promotion, then truncated back to `u16` — every intermediate is in `0..=7` so the truncation is exact. `HAVE_INLINE_ASM` is undefined, so no asm barrier is emitted.\n\nI checked that `quirks.h` renames only the argon2 `*_verify` functions, not `crypto_verify_*`, and does not touch any runtime symbol.\n\n## Verification\n\n`nm -D --defined-only` on the built `.so` shows exactly the 19 expected symbols from these two files and no extras. A C driver linked against the `.so` confirms: `_bytes()` return 16/32/64; equal buffers give 0; every single-bit flip and every full-byte difference at all 64 positions gives -1; `_sodium_runtime_get_cpu_features()` returns -1; all twelve `has_*` return 0.\n\nI did not modify any file other than `src/runtime.rs` and `src/verify.rs`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":280,"cache_read_input_tokens":50945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":280,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MfPx5kiHmbD32AKQMBfeMJ","session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706753ef0ef","uuid":"aa832925-37a4-45a3-bb47-498be04c9f27","timestamp":"2026-08