YMBOLS (exactly these three, from `src/ed25519_ref10/fe.rs`):\n  `_sodium_fe25519_frombytes`, `_sodium_fe25519_tobytes`, `_sodium_fe25519_invert`\n(`private/quirks.h` renames `fe25519_frombytes`/`fe25519_tobytes`/`fe25519_invert`).\nDeclare them as:\n  #[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_frombytes(h: *mut i32, s: *const u8)\n  #[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_tobytes(s: *mut u8, h: *const i32)\n  #[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_invert(out: *mut i32, z: *const i32)\n(A C `fe25519` parameter decays to `int32_t *`.)\n\nALL other fe25519 functions must ALSO be provided as `pub` (non-`no_mangle`) Rust\nfunctions so that the sibling modules `src/ed25519_ref10/{ge,sc,h2c,ristretto}.rs`\ncan call them. Use this EXACT naming and signature convention (out-params first,\nmirroring the C):\n\n```rust\npub fn fe25519_0(h: &mut Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_1(h: &mut Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_add(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sub(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_neg(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_cmov(f: &mut Fe25519, g: &Fe25519, b: u32);\npub fn fe25519_cswap(f: &mut Fe25519, g: &mut Fe25519, b: u32);\npub fn fe25519_copy(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_isnegative(f: &Fe25519) -> i32;\npub fn fe25519_iszero(f: &Fe25519) -> i32;\npub fn fe25519_mul(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sq(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sq2(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_mul32(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519, n: u32);\npub fn fe25519_frombytes(h: &mut Fe25519, s: &[u8; 32]);   // or *const u8 slice-safe helper\npub fn fe25519_reduce(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_tobytes(s: &mut [u8; 32], h: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sqmul(s: &mut Fe25519, n: i32, a: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_invert(out: &mut Fe25519, z: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_pow22523(out: &mut Fe25519, z: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_cneg(h: &mut Fe25519, b: u32);\npub fn fe25519_abs(h: &mut Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_unchecked_sqrt(x: &mut Fe25519, x2: &Fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sqrt(x: &mut Fe25519, x2: &Fe25519) -> i32;\npub fn fe25519_notsquare(x: &Fe25519) -> i32;\n```\nIMPORTANT ALIASING NOTE: the C code frequently calls e.g. `fe25519_mul(h, h, g)` or\n`fe25519_sq(s, s)` where the output aliases an input. `&mut` + `&` to the same array is\nUB/impossible in safe Rust. Therefore implement each function by FIRST copying the inputs\ninto local `[i32;10]`/`[i64;10]` variables (which the C code effectively does anyway since\nit loads all limbs into locals before writing any output) and THEN writing the output.\nTo make aliasing calls expressible, ALSO provide raw-pointer variants used internally:\n```rust\npub unsafe fn fe25519_mul_p(h: *mut i32, f: *const i32, g: *const i32);\n```\n…OR (preferred, simpler) make the `&mut`/`&` versions take VALUES for the inputs:\n```rust\npub fn fe25519_mul(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519)\n```\nand additionally export convenience value-returning helpers\n```rust\npub fn fe_mul(f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_sq(f: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_sq2(f: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_add(f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_sub(f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_neg(f: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_mul32(f: &Fe25519, n: u32) -> Fe25519;\n```\nProvide BOTH forms (the `&mut`-out form implemented on top of the value form) so\nsibling modules have a convenient, aliasing-safe API. Document them at the top of\nthe file in a short comment block so the other agents can see the API.\n\nFIDELITY REQUIREMENTS (critical — this is the core of ed25519):\n- The limb representation is 10 signed 32-bit limbs with alternating 26/25-bit sizes.\n- `fe25519_mul`/`fe25519_sq`/`fe25519_sq2` in the C use `int64_t` intermediates with\n  precomputed `2*f1`, `19*g9`, `38*f9` etc. Transcribe EVERY li