bs into locals before writing any output) and THEN writing the output.\nTo make aliasing calls expressible, ALSO provide raw-pointer variants used internally:\n```rust\npub unsafe fn fe25519_mul_p(h: *mut i32, f: *const i32, g: *const i32);\n```\n…OR (preferred, simpler) make the `&mut`/`&` versions take VALUES for the inputs:\n```rust\npub fn fe25519_mul(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519)\n```\nand additionally export convenience value-returning helpers\n```rust\npub fn fe_mul(f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_sq(f: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_sq2(f: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_add(f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_sub(f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_neg(f: &Fe25519) -> Fe25519;\npub fn fe_mul32(f: &Fe25519, n: u32) -> Fe25519;\n```\nProvide BOTH forms (the `&mut`-out form implemented on top of the value form) so\nsibling modules have a convenient, aliasing-safe API. Document them at the top of\nthe file in a short comment block so the other agents can see the API.\n\nFIDELITY REQUIREMENTS (critical — this is the core of ed25519):\n- The limb representation is 10 signed 32-bit limbs with alternating 26/25-bit sizes.\n- `fe25519_mul`/`fe25519_sq`/`fe25519_sq2` in the C use `int64_t` intermediates with\n  precomputed `2*f1`, `19*g9`, `38*f9` etc. Transcribe EVERY line exactly. Use\n  `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add` on i64 and the exact same shift/mask carry chain\n  (`carry0 = (h0 + (int64_t)(1 << 25)) >> 26;` etc.). Note C's `>>` on signed\n  negative values is an arithmetic shift — Rust's `>>` on `i64` is also arithmetic, so\n  this maps directly.\n- `fe25519_tobytes` carry-propagation and the `q = (19 * h9 + (((int32_t) 1) << 24)) >> 25;`\n  logic must be exact.\n- `fe25519_frombytes` masks the top byte with 0x7f  (`load_4(s + 28) & 8388607`).\n- `fe25519_cmov`/`cswap` use `b = (unsigned int) (-(int) b);` masking — reproduce exactly\n  (constant-time, no branches).\n- `fe25519_notsquare` uses `FE25519_