{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rzctdmzonlxd3erxb4fqrkza5ubyn67ya4bbujm455j7rusxdaha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`src/softaes.rs` is fully written and verified.\n\n## Exported symbols (9, exactly matching SYMBOLS.md)\n\n- `_sodium_softaes_expand_key128`\n- `_sodium_softaes_expand_key256`\n- `_sodium_softaes_inv_mix_columns`\n- `_sodium_softaes_invert_key_schedule128`\n- `_sodium_softaes_invert_key_schedule256`\n- `_sodium_softaes_block_encrypt`\n- `_sodium_softaes_block_encryptlast`\n- `_sodium_softaes_block_decrypt`\n- `_sodium_softaes_block_decryptlast`\n\nAll are `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"`. `SoftAesBlock` is `#[repr(C)]` with the exact 4×`u32` layout from `private/softaes.h`, so the by-value struct returns use the C ABI.\n\n## Preprocessor path chosen\n\n`FAVOR_PERFORMANCE` is **not** defined (no `__wasm__`, nothing in the build defines it), so I translated the `#else` branch: the SRM-1R bitsliced, table-free round for `softaes_block_encrypt` (`srm1r_*` helpers, `srm1r_subbytes`, `srm1r_mix_columns`) and the strided/`SOFTAES_STRIDE = 16` variant of `softaes_block_encryptlast`. The 1024-entry `_aes_lut` T-table and the `LUT0..LUT3` pointers exist only in the `FAVOR_PERFORMANCE` branch and are therefore **not** present in the Rust file (correctly so).\n\n## Table counts verified\n\n| Table | C | Rust | Values byte-identical |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SBOX` | 256 | 256 | yes |\n| `RCON` | 11 | 11 | yes |\n| `INV_SBOX` | 256 | 256 | yes |\n\n(The C file defines `INV_SBOX` twice, once per `#if` branch; I confirmed the two definitions are identical, so a single Rust `static` is faithful.) Tables were machine-extracted from the C source and diffed element-by-element, not transcribed by hand.\n\n## Build status\n\n`CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt_softaes cargo build --release` produces **zero errors and zero warnings mentioning `src/softaes.rs`**. The crate build still stops on pre-existing errors in other agents' files (`src/ed25519_ref10/tables.rs` — missing `Fe25519`/`Ge25519Precomp`; `src/hash_sha512_cp.rs` — `[u8; 128]` type mismatch); those are outside my assignment and I did not touch them.\n\n## Functional self-check\n\nBuilt a scratch crate at `$TMPDIR/aescheck` that compiles `src/softaes.rs` standalone (with a stubbed `crate::common`) and drives full AES through the exported round functions. All FIPS-197 vectors pass:\n\n- AES-128, key `000102…0f`, pt `00112233…ff` → `69c4e0d86a7b0430d8cdb78070b4c55a` (expected)\n- AES-256, key `000102…1f`, same pt → `8ea2b7ca516745bfeafc49904b496089` (expected)\n- Both decrypt round-trips (via `invert_key_schedule*` + `block_decrypt` + `block_decryptlast`) recover the plaintext, which also exercises `inv_mix_columns`.\n- `_sodium_softaes_inv_mix_columns(0xbca14d8e)` returned `0x455313db`, the correct inverse of the NIST MixColumns example. (One assertion in my scratch driver tripped only because I typo'd the expected literal as `0x453513db`; the function output is right.)\n\nOnly `src/softaes.rs` was modified; scratch artifacts live under `$TMPDIR`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":84933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":596,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ema8BQtWrK9LX4VcX82tm6","session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706753ef0ef","uuid":"c2cfde0c-888b-4509-b31a-4e8353a5555f","timestamp":"2026-08-22T13:44:33.195Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate softaes"}
