{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_b3eu6wplyuc4xedpfuixl2yiccqsowly3i4x7a7cb5c3w4uwneia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three files are written and verified.\n\n## Exported symbols per file\n\n**`src/keccak1600_ref.rs`** (from `crypto_core/keccak1600/ref/keccak1600_ref.c`) — 5 symbols, all `_sodium_`-prefixed per `private/quirks.h`:\n- `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_init`\n- `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_xor_bytes`\n- `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_extract_bytes`\n- `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_permute_24`\n- `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_permute_12`\n\nPrivate items: `KECCAK_ROUND_CONSTANTS`, lane-index constants, `keccak_prepare_theta`, `keccak_theta_rho_pi_chi_iota_pre`, `keccak_theta_rho_pi_chi_iota`, `keccakf_24_rounds`, `keccakf_12_rounds`. The C's `KECCAK_DECLARE_STATE`/`A`↔`E` alternating macros are mapped to two `[u64; 25]` arrays plus a `[u64; 5]` column-parity array; `rotl64`/`load64_le`/`store64_le` come from `crate::common`.\n\n**`src/keccak1600.rs`** (from `crypto_core/keccak1600/keccak1600.c`) — 6 symbols:\n- `crypto_core_keccak1600_statebytes`, `_init`, `_xor_bytes`, `_extract_bytes`, `_permute_24`, `_permute_12`\n\nAlso defines the public `#[repr(C, align(16))] crypto_core_keccak1600_state { opaque: [u8; 224] }`. `__ARM_FEATURE_SHA3` is undefined in the reference build, so the dispatch macros resolve to the `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_*` functions, declared in a local `extern \"C\"` block.\n\n**`src/hash_sha3.rs`** (from `crypto_hash/sha3/hash_sha3.c`) — 12 symbols:\n- `crypto_hash_sha3256`, `_bytes`, `_statebytes`, `_init`, `_update`, `_final`\n- `crypto_hash_sha3512`, `_bytes`, `_statebytes`, `_init`, `_update`, `_final`\n\nNote: there is **no** SHA3-384 in this C file (the assignment brief mentioned `_384`; neither `hash_sha3.c` nor `crypto_hash_sha3.h` nor SYMBOLS.md contains it), and the linker names are `crypto_hash_sha3256_*` / `crypto_hash_sha3512_*` (no underscore before the digit). Private `sha3_init`/`sha3_update`/`sha3_final` plus `sha3_state_internal`; cross-file calls to `crypto_core_keccak1600_*` and `sodium_memzero` go through a local `extern \"C\"` block.\n\n## Layout verification (gcc vs. Rust)\nConfirmed identical with a C probe program: `crypto_core_keccak1600_state` = 224 bytes / align 16; `crypto_hash_sha3{256,512}_state` = 256 / 16; `sha3_state_internal` = 256 / 16 with field offsets 224 (`offset`), 232 (`rate`), 240 (`outlen`), 248 (`phase`). The two `COMPILER_ASSERT`s are reproduced as `const _: () = assert!(...)`.\n\n## Correctness\nCompiled the three modules in isolation (clean, zero warnings) and ran differential tests:\n- NIST vectors match: SHA3-256/512 of `\"\"`, `\"abc\"`, and 200×`0xa3`.\n- Built the actual C `keccak1600.c` + `keccak1600_ref.c` with gcc and compared byte-for-byte: `permute_12` and `permute_24` on a zeroed state, and a mixed unaligned/aligned/tail `xor_bytes` sequence (offset 3 len 100, then offset 103 len 97) — all three digests identical to the Rust output.\n- Streaming consistency: `init`/`update`/`final` in chunk sizes 1, 3, 17, 64, 71, 72, 73, 136, 199 matches the one-shot hash across input lengths 0, 1, 71, 72, 73, 135, 136, 137, 200, 271, 272, 500 (covers both rate boundaries).\n\n## Build status\n`cargo build --release` reports no errors in `keccak1600_ref.rs`, `keccak1600.rs`, or `hash_sha3.rs`. The 3 remaining crate-wide errors are in other agents' files (`src/ed25519_ref10/tables.rs`, `src/hash_sha256.rs:28`, `src/hash_sha512_cp.rs:295` — the last is a real bug: `static PAD: [u8; 128]` initialized with 129 elements). A cdylib built from just my three modules exports exactly the 23 symbols listed in SYMBOLS.md, no more and no fewer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":387,"cache_read_input_tokens":80343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":387,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"