itions use `wrapping_add`.\n- Transform signatures keep the C shape `(state, block, W, S)` with `W = &tmp[0]`, `S = &tmp[64]` (resp. `&tmp[80]`), so no aliasing/borrow issues; state fields are reached via `core::ptr::addr_of_mut!`.\n- The `for (i = 0; i < 64; i += 16)` loop with `if (i == 48) break;` before the `MSCH` block is reproduced with the increment placed after `MSCH` (equivalent since `break` is the only other exit).\n- Cross-file: `sodium_memzero` (and `crypto_hash_sha512` in `crypto_hash.rs`) declared in local `extern \"C\"` blocks; only `crate::common::{load32_be, store32_be, store64_be, rotr32, load64_be, store64_be, rotr64}` imported.\n- `hash_sha256.rs`/`hash_sha512.rs`/`crypto_hash.rs` carry their own `#[repr(C)]` state-struct copies so files stay independent; `size_of` yields 104 / 208.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt_sha cargo build --release`: zero errors/warnings referencing my five files. The one remaining crate-wide error is `src/ed25519_ref10/tables.rs:3` (`unresolved imports super::Fe25519, super::Ge25519Precomp`) — another agent's file, so the `.so` cannot link yet.\n- Standalone harness (`include!`-ing my files, since the crate is a cdylib) confirmed against FIPS 180-4 vectors: sha256(\"abc\") = `ba7816bf…f20015ad`, sha512(\"abc\") = `ddaf35a1…a54ca49f`, sha256/sha512 of \"\" , of the 56-byte and 112-byte NIST messages, and of 1,000,000 `'a'` (`cdc76e5c…` / `e718483d…`) — all exact. Random-chunk streaming (`init`/`update`×N/`final`) matches the one-shot digest for both. `crypto_hash(\"abc\")` equals sha512, `crypto_hash_bytes()` = 64, `crypto_hash_primitive()` = `\"sha512\"`.\n- Struct layout cross-checked against a C program compiled with the real headers: sha256 size 104, offsets 0/32/40; sha512 size 208, offsets 0/64/80 — identical to the Rust `#[repr(C)]` structs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1044,"cache_read_input_tokens":831