_*_MEMORY_FENCES`), so it is dropped.\n- Local `strchr` reproduces C semantics including a search for `\\0` matching the terminator — this matters, because a NUL byte in `hex`/`b64` falls into the \"not a valid digit\" branch and is then treated as ignorable whenever `ignore != NULL`.\n- `sodium_base64_ENCODED_LEN` is reproduced as a private helper, including the `unsigned int` → `size_t` zero-extension of `(0U - (((VARIANT) & 2U) >> 1))` before the AND with `(3U - rem)`.\n- `parse_ipv6` uses `usize` offsets into `tmp` rather than raw pointers so the C's `tp + 2 > endp` / `tp + 4 > endp` one-past-the-end arithmetic stays well-defined in Rust while computing identical results.\n- `buf` in `sodium_bin2ip` is zero-initialized: the C `memcpy(ip, buf, len + 1U)` on the IPv4-mapped path copies one indeterminate byte, which `ip[len] = 0` immediately overwrites, so behavior is identical without the UB.\n- `assert(b64_pos <= b64_len)` became `debug_assert!` (compiled out under the crate's `debug-assertions = false`, matching `NDEBUG`).\n- All arithmetic uses explicit `wrapping_*` / `wrapping_shl` / `wrapping_shr` with the C truncation to `unsigned char`/`unsigned int` written out at each step."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":77242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":596,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018zT4DuCwuf3th2AbhctrrK","session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706753ef0ef","uuid":"6be03374-12e5-4d3b-a03c-5c1a6a7d17f1","timestamp":"2026-08-22T13:44:57.913Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate sodium/codecs.c"}
