{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bqukmi7sfssk3ueywoolixkf74i6qrlcg6uouuoku2nbje7rgc4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_018REAsxSsCFnaaihdG3mFmu","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Translate sc25519 mul and muladd","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are translating libsodium 1.0.23 from C to Rust.\n\nWorking directory (crate root): /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-Vjhgd4/translated_rust\n\nFIRST read `CONTRACT.md` in the crate root, and `src/ed25519_ref10/mod.rs`\n(it provides `pub unsafe fn load_3(input: *const u8) -> u64` and\n`pub unsafe fn load_4(input: *const u8) -> u64` — use those; do NOT edit mod.rs).\n\nYOUR ASSIGNMENT — write **only** the file `src/ed25519_ref10/sc_mul.rs`.\n\nTranslate these two functions from\n`c_src/libsodium/crypto_core/ed25519/ref10/ed25519_ref10.c`:\n\n  * `sc25519_mul`    — source lines 1194..1661 (about 460 lines of fully unrolled\n                       schoolbook multiplication + Barrett reduction)\n  * `sc25519_muladd` — source lines 1663..2149 (about 480 lines, same shape)\n\nThese are enormous, fully-unrolled integer routines with hundreds of statements of the\nform\n```c\n    s0  = 2097151 & load_3(a);\n    s1  = 2097151 & (load_4(a + 2) >> 5);\n    ...\n    a0b0 = a0 * (int64_t) b0;\n    ...\n    carry0 = (s0 + (int64_t) (1L << 20)) >> 21; s1 += carry0; s0 -= carry0 * ((uint64_t) 1L << 21);\n    ...\n    s[0] = (unsigned char) (s0 >> 0);\n```\nTRANSCRIBE EVERY SINGLE LINE MECHANICALLY AND EXACTLY. Do not \"simplify\", do not write a\nloop where the C is unrolled, do not reorder. A single dropped or reordered statement\nsilently breaks Ed25519 signing.\n\nSTRONGLY RECOMMENDED APPROACH — do it with a script, not by hand:\nWrite a small Python script that reads the exact line range from the C file and emits Rust:\n  - `int64_t x;`  declarations  -> collect names, emit `let mut x: i64 = 0;`\n  - `s0 = 2097151 & load_3(a);`            -> `s0 = 2097151 & load_3(a) as i64;`\n    (note `load_3` returns u64 in C too; the C assigns to int64_t, so cast)\n  - `load_4(a + 2) >> 5`                    -> `load_4(a.add(2)) >> 5`\n  - `a0*(int64_t) b0`                       -> `a0.wrapping_mul(b0)`\n  - `x += y;`  -> `x = x.wrapping_add(y);`   ;  `x -= y;` -> `x = x.wrapping_sub(y);`\n  - `carry0 * ((uint64_t) 1L << 21)`        -> `carry0.wrapping_mul(1i64 << 21)`\n    (C: `carry0` is int64_t, multiplied by a uint64_t constant 2097152 -> the product is\n     computed in uint64_t then subtracted from an int64_t; because everything is exact\n     modulo 2^64 the `wrapping_mul` on i64 gives identical bits. Verify this reasoning\n     holds for each pattern you encounter.)\n  - `s[0] = (unsigned char) (s0 >> 0);`     -> `*s.add(0) = (s0 >> 0) as u8;`\n  - `(int64_t) 1L << 20`                    -> `1i64 << 20`\n  - `2097151 & ...`                         -> `2097151 & ...`\nThen hand-review a random sample of ~40 emitted lines against the C, and verify the\nstatement COUNT matches (`grep -c ';'` on the C range vs your Rust body).\n\nSIGNATURES (these are `pub` Rust helpers; the exported `extern \"C\"` wrappers live in\n`src/ed25519_ref10/sc.rs`, written by another agent, so do NOT add `#[no_mangle]` here):\n```rust\npub unsafe fn sc25519_mul(s: *mut u8, a: *const u8, b: *const u8);\npub unsafe fn sc25519_muladd(s: *mut u8, a: *const u8, b: *const u8, c: *const u8);\n```\n(The C signatures are `unsigned char s[32]`, `const unsigned char a[32]`, ... which decay\nto pointers.)\n\nDo NOT edit any file other than `src/ed25519_ref10/sc_mul.rs`.\n\nVerify with:\n  CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt_scmul cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E '^error' -A6 | head -80\nIterate until no error mentions sc_mul.rs.\n\nMANDATORY SELF-CHECK: build a differential harness. Compile the C `ed25519_ref10.c`\ndirectly (it needs `-Ic_src/libsodium/include -Ic_src/libsodium/include/sodium\n-Ic_src/libsodium/crypto_core/ed25519/ref10 -Ic_src/libsodium/crypto_verify`) into a\nshared object, and a Rust cdylib that `include!`s your sc_mul.rs (with tiny `load_3`/\n`load_4` shims). Feed 10000 random 32-byte inputs to both `_sodium_sc25519_mul` /\n`_sodium_sc25519_muladd` and compare the 32 output bytes byte-for-byte. Report the result.\nIf a full harness is impractical, at minimum verify with the known vector:\n  sc25519_mul(1, 1) == 1 and sc25519_muladd(a, 0, 0, c) == c reduced mod L.\n\nReport: statement counts (C vs Rust) for each function, self-check outcome, and clean\nbuild confirmation for your file."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":631,"cache_read_input_tokens":148075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":631,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706753ef0ef","uuid":"24717bb7-92c8-42d8-b5c4-8b590d299587","timestamp":"2026-08-22T13:45:42.553Z"}
