{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jyt444heuvp2om3salarpqwtia56gyfmttgjo26qdspachbazjta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All nine files are translated and verified.\n\n## Files and exported symbols\n\n| File | Exported symbols |\n|---|---|\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-Vjhgd4/translated_rust/src/poly1305_donna.rs` | `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_donna_implementation` (data, 0x28 bytes) |\n| `.../src/onetimeauth_poly1305.rs` | `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305`, `_verify`, `_init`, `_update`, `_final`, `_bytes`, `_keybytes`, `_statebytes`, `_keygen`, `_crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_pick_best_implementation` |\n| `.../src/crypto_onetimeauth.rs` | `crypto_onetimeauth`, `_verify`, `_init`, `_update`, `_final`, `_bytes`, `_keybytes`, `_statebytes`, `_primitive`, `_keygen` |\n| `.../src/shorthash_siphash24_ref.rs` | `crypto_shorthash_siphash24` |\n| `.../src/shorthash_siphashx24_ref.rs` | `crypto_shorthash_siphashx24` |\n| `.../src/shorthash_siphash24.rs` | `crypto_shorthash_siphash24_bytes`, `crypto_shorthash_siphash24_keybytes` |\n| `.../src/shorthash_siphashx24.rs` | `crypto_shorthash_siphashx24_bytes`, `crypto_shorthash_siphashx24_keybytes` |\n| `.../src/crypto_shorthash.rs` | `crypto_shorthash`, `_bytes`, `_keybytes`, `_primitive`, `_keygen` |\n| `.../src/crypto_auth.rs` | `crypto_auth`, `_verify`, `_bytes`, `_keybytes`, `_primitive`, `_keygen` |\n\nThis matches the SYMBOLS.md sections exactly (verified with `nm -D --defined-only`), no extras, no omissions. `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_donna_implementation` is `D` with size `0x28`.\n\n## Key finding worth noting\n\nThe task brief said the 32-bit Poly1305 uses `uint32_t h[5], r[5], pad[4]`. That is **wrong for this target**: `poly1305_donna32.h` declares them as `unsigned long`, which is **64-bit** on x86-64 Linux. I confirmed via `gcc -E` (donna32.h is indeed selected, `HAVE_TI_MODE` undefined) and `sizeof`/`_Alignof` (struct is **144 bytes, align 8**, well under the 256-byte opaque state). All limb arithmetic is therefore reproduced in `u64` with `wrapping_*`, and in particular `mask = (g4 >> (sizeof(unsigned long)*8 - 1)) - 1` is a **shift by 63**, not 31. Using `u32` would have produced wrong MACs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release`: clean, zero errors and zero warnings (crate-wide fresh build).\n- Differential test against the actual C reference: compiled `poly1305_donna.c`, `shorthash_siphash24_ref.c`, `shorthash_siphashx24_ref.c` with gcc (symbols renamed via `-D` to avoid collision) and `dlopen`ed the Rust `.so`. 4000 randomized trials, lengths 0..560:\n  - one-shot Poly1305 tags, `verify` positive and negative results,\n  - incremental `init`/`update`/`final` with random 1..39-byte chunks (exercises the `leftover` buffering paths),\n  - the full 256-byte state buffer after `final` byte-for-byte (confirms `sodium_memzero` zeroes exactly the 144 bytes the C does and leaves the rest untouched),\n  - `crypto_shorthash_siphash24` and `crypto_shorthash_siphashx24` outputs.\n  All matched. Plus the RFC 8439 Poly1305 vector and the SipHash-2-4 empty-input vector pass.\n- Wrapper test: all `*_bytes`/`*_keybytes`/`*_statebytes` (256 for state) and `*_primitive` strings (`\"poly1305\"`, `\"siphash24\"`, `\"hmacsha512256\"`) correct; `crypto_shorthash`/`crypto_onetimeauth`/`crypto_auth` forward to the right primitives; `crypto_auth_verify` positive/negative correct; all four `*_keygen` functions write random bytes; `_crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_pick_best_implementation()` returns 0 and leaves behaviour unchanged.\n\nNo files outside my nine were modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":102987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":686,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id"