{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012suFkiqZr119HNg9wz2ayD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#ifndef argon2_encoding_H\n2\t#define argon2_encoding_H\n3\t\n4\t#include \"argon2.h\"\n5\t#include \"private/quirks.h\"\n6\t\n7\t/*\n8\t * encode an Argon2 hash string into the provided buffer. 'dst_len'\n9\t * contains the size, in characters, of the 'dst' buffer; if 'dst_len'\n10\t * is less than the number of required characters (including the\n11\t * terminating 0), then this function returns 0.\n12\t *\n13\t * if ctx->outlen is 0, then the hash string will be a salt string\n14\t * (no output). if ctx->saltlen is also 0, then the string will be a\n15\t * parameter-only string (no salt and no output).\n16\t *\n17\t * On success, ARGON2_OK is returned.\n18\t *\n19\t * No other parameters are checked\n20\t */\n21\tint argon2_encode_string(char *dst, size_t dst_len, argon2_context *ctx,\n22\t                         argon2_type type);\n23\t\n24\t/*\n25\t * Decodes an Argon2 hash string into the provided structure 'ctx'.\n26\t * The fields ctx.saltlen, ctx.adlen, ctx.outlen set the maximal salt, ad, out\n27\t * length values\n28\t * that are allowed; invalid input string causes an error\n29\t *\n30\t * Returned value is ARGON2_OK on success.\n31\t */\n32\tint argon2_decode_string(argon2_context *ctx, const char *str,\n33\t                         argon2_type type);\n34\t\n35\t#endif\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AqA8AJbtvvpbdQxEY3Mv1j","session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706753ef0ef","uuid":"713256dd-24cc-407f-826c-1a345540dba4","timestamp":"2026-08-22T13:50:51.436Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate argon2 API and pwhash"}
