rd bookkeeping EXACTLY, with `wrapping_add` and\n  `crate::common::{load32_le, store32_le, rotl32}` (or the file's own `le32dec/le32enc`).\n  Note the `uint32_t X[16]` alignment and the `#ifdef` for `HAVE_EMMINTRIN_H` is absent.\n- `crypto_scrypt-common.c` implements `escrypt_r` (the `$7$` string format),\n  `escrypt_gensalt_r`, `escrypt_parse_setting`, and the itoa64 encode/decode.\n  Copy the `itoa64` alphabet string EXACTLY.\n- `pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256.c`: `crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256`,\n  `_str`, `_str_verify`, `_str_needs_rehash`, `_ll`, and all the `_bytes_*`/`_saltbytes`/\n  `_strbytes`/`_strprefix`/`_opslimit_*`/`_memlimit_*`/`_passwd_*` accessors, plus\n  `pickparams`/`crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256_ll`. Preserve the exact\n  `errno`/`EINVAL`/`EFBIG`/`ENOMEM` values and check order. Declare `__errno_location`.\n- Cross-file: `crypto_auth_hmacsha256*`, `crypto_hash_sha256*`, `sodium_memzero`,\n  `sodium_malloc`, `sodium_free`, `sodium_memcmp`, `randombytes_buf`, `sodium_misuse`,\n  `malloc`, `free`, `sysconf`, `mmap`, `munmap` — local `extern \"C\"` blocks as needed.\n\nDeliverables: the five .rs files fully written (no TODOs, no stubs), exporting exactly the\nsymbols listed in SYMBOLS.md for those five C files.\n\nVerify by running (from the crate root):\n  CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt_scrypt cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E '^error' -A6 | head -100\nOnly errors mentioning your five files are yours. Do NOT edit any other file.\n\nReport at the end: the list of exported symbol names you defined per file, and\nconfirmation that the build has no errors in your files."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2953,"cache_read_input_tokens":190460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2953,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706