 by building the five files plus `common.rs` as a standalone cdylib and running `nm -D --defined-only`; the temp crate was removed afterwards).\n\n## Build status\n`cargo build --release` on the full crate reports 16 errors, **none in my five files**. All remaining errors are in other agents' files: `src/crypto_secretbox_easy.rs`, `src/secretbox_xchacha20poly1305.rs` (cast-vs-generic `as u64 <` parse issues), and `src/randombytes_internal_random.rs` (`stream` name collision, undefined `ret`). Because the crate could not link, I also compiled my five files in isolation — they build clean with zero errors and zero warnings.\n\n## Notes / deviations from the task briefing\n- **`open.c` in 1.0.23 differs from the briefing.** There is no `crypto_verify_32(sig, rcheck)` and no `ge25519_tobytes`. The actual check order is: `(sig[63] & 240) != 0 && sc25519_is_canonical(sig+32) == 0` → `ge25519_is_canonical(pk) == 0` → `ge25519_frombytes_negate_vartime(&A, pk) != 0 || ge25519_has_small_order(&A) != 0` → `ge25519_frombytes(&expected_r, sig) != 0 || ge25519_has_small_order(&expected_r) != 0`, then hash/reduce, `ge25519_double_scalarmult_vartime` → `ge25519_p2_to_p3` → `ge25519_p3_sub`, and the return value is `ge25519_has_small_order(&check) - 1`. I translated the source, not the briefing. This adds externs `_sodium_ge25519_frombytes`, `_sodium_ge25519_p2_to_p3`, `_sodium_ge25519_p3_sub` and drops `crypto_verify_32`/`_sodium_ge25519_tobytes`. Note `ge25519_has_small_order` takes `const ge25519_p3 *`, not a byte array, in this version.\n- `ACQUIRE_FENCE` expands to `(void) 0` (no `HAVE_*_MEMORY_FENCES` without `config.h`), so it is a comment.\n- `keypair.c` needs `fe25519_1`/`fe25519_add`/`fe25519_sub`/`fe25519_mul`, which are `static`/`static inline` in `private/ed25519_ref10_fe_25_5.h`; per the contract I duplicated them as private helpers in `src/keypair.rs` (with explicit wrapping arithmetic, including the `(uint64_t) 1L << 26` unsigned-subtraction quirks in the carry chain).\n- `ED25519_NONDETERMINISTIC` and `ED25519_COMPAT` are both undefined, so only the deterministic-nonce and canonicality-checking paths are present.\n- All 21 cross-file externs I declare were confirmed present in `.c_syms.txt`, so linking will resolve once the other files compile.","usage":{"total_tokens":103667,"tool_uses":41,"duration_ms":443466},"uuid":"4478fc4f-b535-4e85-af69-586661364d22","session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706753ef0ef"}
