{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7qb7mwiv3ejxygqvnecp5t65f2hzyu65ceojzr6obqz5z23sh33q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files are written, type-check cleanly, and were verified bit-for-bit against the compiled C reference.\n\n## `src/ed25519_ref10/h2c.rs`\nC source: `ed25519_ref10.c` lines 2595–2762.\n\nExported symbols (exactly 3, matching SYMBOLS.md):\n- `_sodium_ge25519_clear_cofactor(p3: *mut Ge25519P3)`\n- `_sodium_ge25519_from_uniform(s: *mut u8, r: *const u8)`\n- `_sodium_ge25519_from_hash(s: *mut u8, h: *const u8)`\n\n`pub` Rust API for siblings:\n- `pub fn ge25519_clear_cofactor(p3: &mut Ge25519P3)`\n- `pub unsafe fn ge25519_from_uniform(s: *mut u8, r: *const u8)`\n- `pub unsafe fn ge25519_from_hash(s: *mut u8, h: *const u8)`\n\nPrivate: `ge25519_mont_to_ed`, `ge25519_xmont_to_ymont`, `ge25519_elligator2`, `fe25519_reduce64`, `optblocker_u8`.\n\n## `src/ed25519_ref10/ristretto.rs`\nC source: `ed25519_ref10.c` lines 2764–2992.\n\nExported symbols (exactly 3):\n- `_sodium_ristretto255_frombytes(h: *mut Ge25519P3, s: *const u8) -> c_int`\n- `_sodium_ristretto255_p3_tobytes(s: *mut u8, h: *const Ge25519P3)`\n- `_sodium_ristretto255_from_hash(s: *mut u8, h: *const u8)`\n\n`pub` Rust API for siblings:\n- `pub fn ristretto255_is_canonical(s: *const u8) -> i32`\n- `pub unsafe fn ristretto255_frombytes(h: &mut Ge25519P3, s: *const u8) -> c_int`\n- `pub unsafe fn ristretto255_p3_tobytes(s: *mut u8, h: &Ge25519P3)`\n- `pub unsafe fn ristretto255_from_hash(s: *mut u8, h: *const u8)`\n\nPrivate: `ristretto255_sqrt_ratio_m1`, `ristretto255_elligator`, `optblocker_u8`.\n\n## Notes / corrections to the brief\n- **`fe25519_reduce64` does NOT use `fe25519_mul32`.** The real 1.0.23 code does `fe25519_frombytes` on *both* halves (each masked `[31] &= 0x7f`), adds `1*19 + 1*722` carry-bit terms into limb 0, then `fe_f[i] += 38 * fe_g[i]` for all 10 limbs, then `fe25519_reduce`. Transcribed as written.\n- **`ge25519_from_uniform`'s sign extraction is `x_sign = ((s[31] >> 5) ^ optblocker_u8) >> 2`**, not a plain `>> 7`. libsodium 1.0.23 routes several of these through `static volatile unsigned char optblocker_u8` (also in `ristretto255_is_canonical`'s `e` term). Since that C static is file-scoped and the C file is split across Rust modules, each of my two files has its own private `OPTBLOCKER_U8: AtomicU8 = 0` read via `Ordering::Relaxed` — value-identical, and the read is not optimized away.\n- `ristretto255_is_canonical` is `pub fn` with an internal `unsafe` block, per your spec.\n- The C freely aliases output with input operands (`fe25519_mul(x, x, y)`, `fe25519_reduce(f, f)`). I added a small `#[inline(always)]` value-returning adapter layer over `fe.rs`/`ge.rs` at the top of each file so the operation sequence is identical while satisfying the borrow checker. `fe.rs` exposes `fe25519_frombytes/tobytes` over `&[u8;32]`, so the adapters use `fe::fe_frombytes_ptr` / `fe25519_tobytes` with a `*mut [u8;32]` cast; `ge25519_p3_tobytes` likewise takes `&mut [u8;32]`.\n- `abort()` → `std::process::abort()` in the unreachable `ge25519_xmont_to_ymont != 0` branch.\n\n## Verification\n- `rustc --emit=metadata` over `common.rs` + the whole `ed25519_ref10` module tree: **0 errors, 0 warnings**, and specifically zero diagnostics referencing `h2c.rs` or `ristretto.rs`. (The full `cargo build --release` still fails, but only in unrelated files: `src/crypto_secretbox_easy.rs`, `src/secretbox_xchacha20poly1305.rs` — `as u64 <` parse errors — and `src/randombytes_sysrandom.rs` — private `__assert_fail`/`C_FILE`. None of those are mine.)\n- **Differential test vs. the C build** at `$TMPDIR/cbuild/libsodium.so`: built my modules into a standalone `cdylib`, `dlopen`ed both with `RTLD_LOCAL`, and compared 4000 pseudorandom 64-byte inputs across `ge25519_from_uniform`, `ge25519_from_hash`, `ristretto255_from_hash`, `ristretto255_frombytes` (return value **and** full 160-byte `ge25519_p3` output state), `ristretto255_p3_tobytes` (incl. round-trip), and `ge25519_clear_cofactor` (bytes + full p3 state), plus 300 crafted canonicality edge cases and a further 2048-case sweep over `s[0] ∈ 0..256` × `s[31] ∈ {0x7f,0xff,0x00,0x80}` with all-`0xff`/all-`0x00` bodies. **Result: 0 mismatches.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":107848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":337,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PP5hjd8MDZa5Pe3gSaqcqq","session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8-c706753ef0ef","uuid":"15bda958-855d-450a-a29e-52145e1f41c8","timestamp":"2026-08-22T13:56:44.627Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate ed25519 h2c and ristretto"}
