{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_aepno2wpv4fpvk6b6lrymowjehi4wqv53ubv7l4eizigwzw3rhha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five files are translated, the crate builds cleanly, and the resulting Rust `.so` is byte-identical to the reference C `.so` on a 33,816-line differential test.\n\n## Files written\n\n**`src/aegis128l_soft.rs`** — exports 1 data symbol:\n- `aegis128l_soft_implementation` (D, 0x10 bytes)\n\nContains the fully expanded `aegis128l_common.h` (init / mac / absorb / absorb2 / enc / dec / declast / `encrypt_detached` / `decrypt_detached`) as private items, the `#[repr(C)] SoftAesBlock`, the `static inline` helpers from `private/softaes.h` duplicated as private fns, and an `extern \"C\"` block for the 9 `_sodium_softaes_*` linker names plus `crypto_verify_16/32`.\n\n**`src/aegis256_soft.rs`** — exports 1 data symbol:\n- `aegis256_soft_implementation` (D, 0x10 bytes)\n\n**`src/aead_aegis128l.rs`** — 11 text symbols: `_crypto_aead_aegis128l_pick_best_implementation`, `crypto_aead_aegis128l_{keybytes,nsecbytes,npubbytes,abytes,messagebytes_max,keygen,encrypt,decrypt,encrypt_detached,decrypt_detached}`\n\n**`src/aead_aegis256.rs`** — 11 text symbols: the `aegis256` analogues.\n\n**`src/aead_aes256gcm.rs`** — 17 text symbols: `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_{is_available,keybytes,nsecbytes,npubbytes,abytes,statebytes,messagebytes_max,keygen,encrypt,decrypt,encrypt_detached,decrypt_detached,beforenm,encrypt_afternm,decrypt_afternm,encrypt_detached_afternm,decrypt_detached_afternm}`\n\n`nm` output vs. `SYMBOLS.md` for these five files: **41 expected, 41 actual, exact match** (verified by diff).\n\n## Key findings / decisions\n\n- **Dispatch**: both `_pick_best_implementation` functions reduce to `implementation = &*_soft_implementation; return 0;` — the `HAVE_ARMCRYPTO`/`HAVE_AVXINTRIN_H`+`HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H` blocks are removed by the preprocessor, and `SYMBOLS.md` confirms the aesni/armcrypto files export nothing, so `sodium_runtime_has_aesni/avx/armcrypto` are **not** called (they can't be — the referenced `*_aesni_implementation` structs don't exist). The removed C is preserved as a comment. `implementation` is a `static mut *const T` initialized with `core::ptr::addr_of!(<extern static>)`, which resolves statically.\n- **`aead_aes256gcm.c`**: verified via preprocessor that all nine AEAD entry points set `errno = 38` (`ENOSYS`, via `__errno_location()`) and return `-1`; `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_is_available()` returns `0`. `statebytes()` = `(size_of::<state>() + 15) & !15` = 512.\n- `MESSAGEBYTES_MAX`: aegis128l/aegis256 = `(1<<61)-1` = 2305843009213693951; aes256gcm = `16*(2^32-2)` = 68719476704 (all confirmed equal to the C library's runtime values).\n- `ACQUIRE_FENCE` expands to `(void) 0` in this build (no `HAVE_GCC_MEMORY_FENCES`/`HAVE_C11_MEMORY_FENCES`).\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Built the reference C library (`cmake -S c_src -B $TMPDIR/cb2`).\n2. Wrote a C driver covering 14 `adlen` values × `mlen` 0..160 for both AEGIS variants: combined encrypt (ct+tag hex), combined decrypt round-trip, tag-tamper rejection (return code, `*mlen_p`, output zeroing), `encrypt_detached` mac, `decrypt_detached` with `m == NULL`, short-`clen` rejection, plus all the constant getters and the aes256gcm stub returns.\n3. Ran it against the C `.so` and against the finished Rust `.so`: **identical, 0 lines of diff** (33,816 lines). Also ran an intermediate isolated-crate variant that linked only `_sodium_softaes_block_encrypt`/`crypto_verify_16`/`crypto_verify_32` from C, confirming (via `nm`/`readelf -r`) that my Rust code — not the C library's — was the code under test.\n4. `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt_aegis cargo build --release` now exits 0 with **zero errors and zero warnings** for the whole crate (the earlier failures were in `crypto_secretbox_easy.rs`, `secretbox_xchacha20poly1305.rs`, `randombytes_internal_random.rs`, `ipcrypt_soft.rs` — other agents' files, since f