bytes`.\n\n**`src/core_ed25519.rs`** (21): all `crypto_core_ed25519_*` per SYMBOLS.md, including the `L` order table copied byte-for-byte.\n\n**`src/core_ristretto255.rs`** (20): all `crypto_core_ristretto255_*` per SYMBOLS.md.\n\n**`src/core_h2c.rs`** (1): `_sodium_core_h2c_string_to_hash` with both `expand_message_xmd` instantiations (SHA-256/64-byte block, SHA-512/128-byte block), the `H2C-OVERSIZE-DST-` path, and `errno = EINVAL` default.\n\n## Verification\n- `cargo build --release`: no errors, no warnings.\n- All 63 expected symbols present with matching `T`/`D` types; no private helpers leaked into the dynamic symbol table.\n- Standalone harness: all four RFC 7748 X25519 vectors reproduce exactly, and the small-order blocklist rejects as expected — confirming the hand-copied `fe25519` arithmetic.\n- **Differential test vs. the reference C build** (`$TMPDIR/cbuild/libsodium.so`, dlopen'd side-by-side): **41,228 checks, 0 failures**, covering x25519 (incl. all 9 small-order/high-bit edge inputs), ed25519/ristretto255 scalarmult (valid + garbage points), all scalar arithmetic (incl. zero and all-0xff edge cases), point add/sub, `from_hash`, all `*_from_string` variants for hash_alg 1/2/3, size accessors, `primitive`, `pick_best_implementation`, and `_sodium_core_h2c_string_to_hash` across h_len ∈ {1,32,33,48,64,65,96} × ctx_len ∈ {0,1,17,255,256,300,1000} × 3 algs.\n\nNote: `src/ed25519_ref10/*` was still a stub when I started but was complete by the end of my turn, which is what made the full differential test possible. I did not modify any file outside my eight."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":184209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":434,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GhASPAC7BxVfi2GefPThLn","session_id":"dbed778e-b40b-44c3-aae8